            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "services/phosphor-chassis-power.service",
                    "line": 5,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "sorry minor thing - is this 'Restart=always' common?  That sounds kinda dangerous."
                },
                {
                    "file": "services/phosphor-chassis-power.service",
                    "line": 5,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Adriana Kobylak",
                        "email": "anoo@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "anoo1"
                    },
                    "message": "I talked with Shawn and Derek about restart policy. Some of the power services such as the regulators one have a restart policy set to 'on-failure', which only differs from 'always' in that it doesn't restart on good path - https://www.freedesktop.org/software/systemd/man/latest/systemd.service.html#Restart=\n\nWe discussed setting a restart policy is probably ok since we want these power apps to always be running, and openbmc has a rate limiting policy where if a service restarts multiple times in a certain amount of time it gets disabled."
                },
                {
                    "file": "services/phosphor-chassis-power.service",
                    "line": 5,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                }
            ],
